OpenID Connect sign-in for the OPNsense web GUI.

Adds a sign-in link to the login page. The link sends the browser to an
OpenID Provider with the authorization code flow and PKCE; on return the
plugin exchanges the code at the token endpoint and starts the web GUI
session for the local user the ID token names.

Only users that already exist on the firewall can sign in. Their groups
and privileges stay as configured. Password sign-in, SSH and the console
are unchanged.
